            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "There is [`MiniHipatterns.get_enabled_buffers()`](https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-hipatterns.html#minihipatterns.get_enabled_buffers) that can be used to check if the buffer is enabled. It didn't look like a good idea to also have something that returns a data for a buffer only.\r\n\r\nAlthough in retrospect it might have been a better approach. Something along the lines of `MiniDiff.get_buf_data()`.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">There is <a href=\"https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-hipatterns.html#minihipatterns.get_enabled_buffers\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">MiniHipatterns.get_enabled_buffers()</code></a> that can be used to check if the buffer is enabled. It didn't look like a good idea to also have something that returns a data for a buffer only.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Although in retrospect it might have been a better approach. Something along the lines of <code class=\"notranslate\">MiniDiff.get_buf_data()</code>.</p>",
            "bodyText": "There is MiniHipatterns.get_enabled_buffers() that can be used to check if the buffer is enabled. It didn't look like a good idea to also have something that returns a data for a buffer only.\nAlthough in retrospect it might have been a better approach. Something along the lines of MiniDiff.get_buf_data().",
